<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1527–1576</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximilian II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg dynasty</a>, reigned from 1564 to 1576. Sympathetic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a>, he granted religious concessions to the Austrian nobility and sought peace within the Empire, while fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. In 1574 he raised the March of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> to a duchy for the Gonzaga of Mantua.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Nicolas Neufchatel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicolas_Neufch%C3%A2tel_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
